# Project-Specific Pattern Violations

Mandatory patterns defined in `@ARCHITECTURE.md` and `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md`.

---

## 1. Direct fetch Usage

**Context:** When making HTTP requests. All API calls must use the centralized `httpClient` factory.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Direct fetch
// src/data/api/UsuarioApi.ts
export const buscarUsuario = async (id: string) => {
  const response = await fetch(`/api/usuarios/${id}`);
  return response.json();
};

// ❌ BAD: Direct axios
// src/presentation/hooks/useVagas.ts
import axios from 'axios';

const useVagas = () => {
  useEffect(() => {
    axios.get('/api/vagas').then(response => {
      setVagas(response.data);
    });
  }, []);
};

// ❌ BAD: fetch in component
// src/presentation/pages/Perfil.tsx
const carregarPerfil = async () => {
  const res = await fetch('/api/perfil', {
    headers: { Authorization: `Bearer ${token}` }
  });
  return res.json();
};
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: httpClient factory
// src/data/api/httpClient.ts
import axios, { AxiosInstance } from 'axios';

export const createHttpClient = (): AxiosInstance => {
  const client = axios.create({
    baseURL: process.env.VITE_API_URL,
    timeout: 30000
  });
  
  // Centralized interceptors
  client.interceptors.request.use(config => {
    const token = store.getState().auth.token;
    if (token) {
      config.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${token}`;
    }
    return config;
  });
  
  client.interceptors.response.use(
    response => response,
    error => {
      // Centralized error handling
      if (error.response?.status === 401) {
        store.dispatch(logout());
      }
      return Promise.reject(error);
    }
  );
  
  return client;
};

// ✅ GOOD: API using httpClient
// src/data/api/UsuarioApi.ts
import { createHttpClient } from './httpClient';

export const usuarioApi = {
  async obterPorId(id: string): Promise<UsuarioResponse> {
    const httpClient = createHttpClient();
    const response = await httpClient.get(`/api/Usuario/Obter/${id}`);
    return response.data.retorno;
  },
  
  async listar(): Promise<UsuarioResponse[]> {
    const httpClient = createHttpClient();
    const response = await httpClient.get('/api/Usuario/Listar');
    return response.data.retorno;
  }
};

// ✅ GOOD: Repository uses API (not HTTP directly)
// src/data/repositories/UsuarioRepositoryImpl.ts
@injectable()
export class UsuarioRepositoryImpl implements UsuarioRepository {
  constructor(
    @inject('UsuarioApi') private api: UsuarioApi
  ) {}
  
  async obterPorId(id: string): Promise<Usuario | null> {
    try {
      const response = await this.api.obterPorId(id);
      return this.mapToDomain(response);
    } catch (error) {
      if (error.response?.status === 404) {
        return null;
      }
      throw error;
    }
  }
}
```

**Why httpClient Factory:**

| Benefit | Description |
|---------|-------------|
| Centralized auth | Token added to all requests automatically |
| Centralized logging | All requests/responses logged consistently |
| Error handling | 401, 500 errors handled in one place |
| Base URL config | Environment-specific URLs in one place |
| Observability | Firebase/analytics tracking in interceptors |
| Retry logic | Can add retry strategies centrally |

**Impact:**

- Loss of traceability - can't track all API calls uniformly
- Observability failure - inconsistent logging/metrics
- Inconsistent logs - some APIs log differently than others
- Security gaps - auth headers added inconsistently
- Maintenance burden - change auth logic in N places

**Detection:**

- `fetch(` anywhere in codebase except core/httpClient
- `axios` imported outside `data/api`
- `import axios from 'axios'` in `.tsx` files
- Check: `grep -r "fetch\|from 'axios'" src/presentation/ src/domain/ src/shared/`

**Architecture Reference:**

See `@ARCHITECTURE.md` Section 3.3: "HTTP Client Factory (createHttpClient) - obrigatorio, nao usar fetch/axios diretamente."

See `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md` Section 1.2: "APIs: Chamadas via httpClient (nao ha fetch() direto)."

