## 3. Breaking Modal Pattern

**Context:** When implementing Dialog/Modal components. Must follow Design System modal structure.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Modal without DialogDescription
// src/presentation/components/vaga/ConfirmarExclusaoModal.tsx
<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
  <DialogContent>
    <DialogHeader>
      <DialogTitle>Confirmar Exclusao</DialogTitle>
      {/* Missing DialogDescription! */}
    </DialogHeader>
    <p>Tem certeza que deseja excluir esta vaga?</p>
    <DialogFooter>
      <Button onClick={onClose}>Cancelar</Button>
      <Button onClick={onConfirm} variant="destructive">Excluir</Button>
    </DialogFooter>
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>

// ❌ BAD: Modal with external logic
// src/presentation/components/feedback/FeedbackModal.tsx
<Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
  <DialogContent>
    {/* Modal contains business orchestration */}
    <EnviarFeedbackFlow /> {/* Complex component inside modal */}
  </DialogContent>
</Dialog>
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Complete modal structure
// src/presentation/components/vaga/ConfirmarExclusaoModal.tsx
import {
  Dialog,
  DialogContent,
  DialogDescription,
  DialogFooter,
  DialogHeader,
  DialogTitle,
} from '@/components/ui/dialog';

interface ConfirmarExclusaoModalProps {
  open: boolean;
  onOpenChange: (open: boolean) => void;
  onConfirm: () => void;
  tituloVaga: string;
}

export const ConfirmarExclusaoModal = ({
  open,
  onOpenChange,
  onConfirm,
  tituloVaga
}: ConfirmarExclusaoModalProps) => {
  return (
    <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Confirmar Exclusao</DialogTitle>
          {/* Required for accessibility */}
          <DialogDescription>
            Tem certeza que deseja excluir a vaga "{tituloVaga}"? 
            Esta acao nao pode ser desfeita.
          </DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>
        
        <DialogFooter>
          <Button variant="outline" onClick={() => onOpenChange(false)}>
            Cancelar
          </Button>
          <Button variant="destructive" onClick={onConfirm}>
            Excluir
          </Button>
        </DialogFooter>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
};

// ✅ GOOD: Modal is thin wrapper, logic outside
// src/presentation/components/feedback/EnviarFeedbackModal.tsx
export const EnviarFeedbackModal = ({
  open,
  onOpenChange,
  onEnviar
}: EnviarFeedbackModalProps) => {
  const [comentario, setComentario] = useState('');
  const [nivel, setNivel] = useState<number>(3);
  
  const handleEnviar = () => {
    onEnviar({ comentario, nivel });
    onOpenChange(false);
  };
  
  return (
    <Dialog open={open} onOpenChange={onOpenChange}>
      <DialogContent>
        <DialogHeader>
          <DialogTitle>Enviar Feedback</DialogTitle>
          <DialogDescription>
            Compartilhe seu feedback sobre este colaborador.
          </DialogDescription>
        </DialogHeader>
        
        {/* Form inside modal - not complex orchestration */}
        <div className="space-y-4">
          <NivelSelector value={nivel} onChange={setNivel} />
          <Textarea 
            value={comentario} 
            onChange={e => setComentario(e.target.value)}
            placeholder="Descreva seu feedback..."
          />
        </div>
        
        <DialogFooter>
          <Button variant="outline" onClick={() => onOpenChange(false)}>
            Cancelar
          </Button>
          <Button onClick={handleEnviar}>
            Enviar
          </Button>
        </DialogFooter>
      </DialogContent>
    </Dialog>
  );
};
```

**Modal Pattern Requirements:**

| Requirement | Implementation |
|-------------|----------------|
| Isolated | Single file per modal in `components/[feature]/modais/` |
| Controlled | Must receive `open` and `onOpenChange` props |
| Accessible | Must include `DialogTitle` and `DialogDescription` |
| Thin | Complex logic delegated to UseCases, not in modal |
| Consistent | Use DS Dialog components (not custom modals) |

**Impact:**

- UI inconsistent - modals look and behave differently
- Difficult maintenance - modal logic scattered
- Accessibility issues - screen readers can't understand modal purpose
- Testing difficulty - complex modals hard to test

**Detection:**

- `<Dialog>` without `<DialogDescription>`
- `grep -L "DialogDescription" src/presentation/components/*/modais/*.tsx`
- Modals with > 100 lines of logic
- Modals importing UseCases directly (should receive callbacks)

**Design System Reference:**

See `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md` Section 1.1: "Modais com `DialogTitle` e `DialogDescription`."

See `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md` Section 1.3: "Modais sem DialogDescription - outros times."

