## 4. Hardcoded Design System Colors

**Context:** When styling components. Must use Design System tokens, not Tailwind colors.

**Forbidden:**

```typescript
// ❌ BAD: Hardcoded Tailwind colors
// src/presentation/components/status/StatusBadge.tsx
const StatusBadge = ({ status }: { status: string }) => {
  return (
    <span className={`
      ${status === 'ativo' ? 'bg-green-100 text-green-800' : ''}
      ${status === 'inativo' ? 'bg-red-100 text-red-800' : ''}
      ${status === 'pendente' ? 'bg-yellow-100 text-yellow-800' : ''}
      ${status === 'info' ? 'bg-blue-100 text-blue-800' : ''}
      px-2 py-1 rounded
    `}>
      {status}
    </span>
  );
};

// ❌ BAD: Direct color values
// src/presentation/pages/recrutamento/GestaoVagas.tsx
<div className="bg-white border-gray-200">
  <h2 className="text-gray-800">Vagas</h2>
</div>

// ❌ BAD: bg-white everywhere
// src/presentation/components/cards/VagaCard.tsx
<Card className="bg-white shadow-md">
```

**Required:**

```typescript
// ✅ GOOD: Design System tokens
// src/presentation/components/status/StatusBadge.tsx
import { Badge } from '@/components/ui/badge';

const StatusBadge = ({ status }: { status: StatusVaga }) => {
  const variants: Record<StatusVaga, 'default' | 'secondary' | 'destructive' | 'outline'> = {
    'ATIVA': 'default',
    'PUBLICADA': 'default',
    'RASCUNHO': 'secondary',
    'EXPIRADA': 'destructive',
    'CANCELADA': 'destructive'
  };
  
  return <Badge variant={variants[status]}>{status}</Badge>;
};

// ✅ GOOD: Semantic tokens
// src/presentation/pages/recrutamento/GestaoVagas.tsx
<div className="bg-surfaceElevated border-borderSoft">
  <h2 className="text-foreground">Vagas</h2>
</div>

// ✅ GOOD: Using Card component from DS
// src/presentation/components/cards/VagaCard.tsx
<Card className="border-borderSoft">
  {/* Card already has correct bg from DS */}
</Card>
```

**Token Mapping:**

| Don't Use (Hardcoded) | Use (DS Token) |
|----------------------|----------------|
| `bg-green-100` | `bg-success/10` or `bg-success` |
| `text-green-800` | `text-success` |
| `bg-red-100` | `bg-destructive/10` |
| `text-red-600` | `text-destructive` |
| `bg-yellow-100` | `bg-warning/10` |
| `bg-blue-100` | `bg-info/10` |
| `bg-white` | `bg-surfaceElevated` or `bg-background` |
| `bg-gray-100` | `bg-muted` |
| `text-gray-800` | `text-foreground` |
| `text-gray-500` | `text-muted-foreground` |
| `border-gray-200` | `border-borderSoft` |

**Impact:**

- Inconsistent UI - some elements don't match DS
- Dark mode breaks - hardcoded colors don't adapt
- Maintenance burden - change requires finding all hardcoded values
- Design debt - drift from approved design

**Detection:**

- `grep -r "bg-green-\|bg-red-\|bg-blue-\|bg-yellow-" src/`
- `grep -r "text-green-\|text-red-\|text-blue-" src/`
- `grep -r "bg-white" src/ --include="*.tsx" | grep -v "design-toolkit"`
- Any color class ending in number (e.g., `-100`, `-800`)

**Design System Reference:**

See `@DESIGN_SYSTEM_AUDIT.md` Section 1.3: "Cores hardcoded (Alta prioridade) - outros times."

See `@public/design-toolkit.md` Section 1.2: "Tokens Estruturais" for all color tokens.

